Question Text (LaTeX):
The most abundant elements by mass in the body of a healthy human adult are: Oxygen (61.4%);
Carbon (22.9%), Hydrogen (10.0%); and Nitrogen (2.6%). The weight which a 75 kg person would
gain if all 1H atoms are replaced by 2H atoms is:

Solution / Explanation:
\textbf{1. Concept \& Formula:}
Combustion analysis: \(\%C = \frac{12}{44} \times \frac{m_{CO_2}}{m_{sample}} \times 100\), \(\%H = \frac{2}{18} \times \frac{m_{H_2O}}{m_{sample}} \times 100\).

\textbf{2. Step-by-Step Derivation:}
Given: \(m_{sample} = 120\,\text{g}\), \(m_{CO_2} = 330\,\text{g}\), \(m_{H_2O} = 270\,\text{g}\).

Calculate \(\%C\):
\[\%C = \frac{12}{44} \times \frac{330}{120} \times 100 = \frac{12 \times 330}{44 \times 120} \times 100 = 75\%\]

Calculate \(\%H\):
\[\%H = \frac{2}{18} \times \frac{270}{120} \times 100 = \frac{2 \times 270}{18 \times 120} \times 100 = 25\%\]

\textbf{3. Conclusion:}
Option (4) is the correct answer.

